# The workshop owns this file: the image creates it once as the workshop's .gitattributes and
# never touches it again. Edit it freely.

# Git stores and checks out every file of the workshop byte for byte, on every machine. Without
# this line a Git for Windows that converts line endings (core.autocrlf, its default) checks the
# workshop out in CRLF: the hooks no longer run ("set: pipefail: invalid option name") before the
# container, at its next start, has put .claude back, a launcher run.sh no longer runs at all, and
# a crew or a dataset no longer has the digest orkeon-bench recorded for it.
# It cuts both ways: git no longer puts in LF a file an editor saved in CRLF. And a file comes
# out as it was committed - run.cmd in CRLF, unless a Git that converted line endings stored it
# in LF before this file existed: `orkeon-bench scaffold <team>` then writes it again.
* -text
